  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Cities  Tram line Ilidza&amp;amp;amp;#150;Hrasnica (f.Sarajevo E-Tram Ext.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Construction of two tram track lines from Ilidza to Hrasnica, including the  construction of a U-turn in Hrasnica (12.96 km in total length), and 20 new  tram stations on this route (the &quot;Project&quot;). The Project also entails  construction of the connection of new tram tracks to the existing ones by  expanding and improving the existing roundabout in Ilidza.  The Project is part of the EBRD&apos;s Green Cities Framework 2 - Window II  Extension 2 (the&quot;Framework&quot;) and was identified as a priority project under the  Canton&apos;s Green City Action Plan (&quot;GCAP&quot;).  The Project&apos;s objectives include reduction of traffic congestion, especially  during the rush hours, by providing better, faster and greener urban transport  service alternatives, thus promoting the shift from the usage of personal  vehicles and diesel buses to cleaner public tram transport service.</narrative>
  </description>
